# Festag — Master Product Prompt (always apply)

Human doc: `docs/festag-master-product-prompt.md`. Ranked below
`festag-master-system-instruction.md` on product direction, authoritative on **how work is done**.

**Build the machine, not screens.** Walk the whole chain before writing code:

```
User → Intent → UI → Interaction → Frontend State → Backend Logic →
Database → AI → Permissions → Notifications → Result → UI feedback
```

## Non-negotiables

- **Objects, states, workflows — never screens.** Every object: identity · owner · status ·
  permissions · timestamps · relationships · lifecycle · actions · history · dependencies.
- **Every UI action has a real consequence.** Define what changes in the DB, who is notified,
  what enters activity, what the user sees next. No fake buttons, no empty interactions.
- **Backend first.** Data, states, permissions, events and AI actions before UI.
- **Never patch broken logic with more UI.** No extra button/modal/status/card on a wrong
  model — fix the model.
- **Decision autonomy tiers** `AUTOMATIC · RECOMMENDED · REQUIRED · BLOCKED` are enforced
  server-side, not merely displayed.
- **Permissions server-side.** Frontend hiding is not security; AI actions respect them too.
- **Tagro** is the intelligence layer — never a chatbot, never "✨ AI Assistant", never a logo.
  It acts through structured actions, not text replies.
- **No black CTA buttons**, no decorative AI gimmicks, no card-grid-everything, no meaningless
  graphs. Primary accent `#5B647D`, base dark `#0F141B`.
- **Mobile is redesigned, not shrunk.** Horizontal scroll is never a responsive fix.
- **Say so when a product decision is bad**, and propose better — do not silently obey.

## Definition of Done

Not "it renders / returns 200 / happy path works". Done means: UX coherent · UI polished ·
backend connected · DB state correct · permissions work · loading + empty + error states exist ·
mobile works · activity logged · notifications where needed · no fake functionality ·
no dead ends.

## Priority order

1. System integrity (DB, permissions, state, backend logic)
2. Core user flows
3. UX (navigation, hierarchy, interactions, states)
4. Visual design

Never polish a screen whose workflow is broken.
